                                              AIMessage(content='我来帮你规划日本5天游。在开始之前，让我先了解一下你的具体需求，这样能规划出更贴合你心意的行程。\n\n首先，让我读取旅行规划技能，并确认一些关键信息。', additional_kwargs={'refusal': None}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 113, 'prompt_tokens': 4433, 'total_tokens': 4546, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cache_write_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 0}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 0, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 4433}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'fp_a18b46594c_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402', 'id': '89f68fbe-238e-4a7e-8537-c5828c7b7087', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None}, name='travel_agent', id='lc_run--019fe579-6ce2-7dd2-9b83-d2305763c4c6-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'read_file', 'args': {'file_path': '/skills/travel-planning/SKILL.md', 'limit': 1000}, 'id': 'call_00_4J9moybM5Voyn9VlZNLi5773', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4433, 'output_tokens': 113, 'total_tokens': 4546, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}, 'output_token_details': {}}),
                                              ToolMessage(content='  1  ---\n  2  name: travel-planning\n  3  description: 创建、重新规划或修改完整旅行行程的专业旅行规划技能。适用于多日旅行规划、每日路线安排、行程调整、旅行节奏、交通与预算设计，以及已有完整行程的修改。仅当用户明确要求规划、安排、重新规划或修改完整旅行时使用；不要用于问候、闲聊、普通旅行问答、单个景点介绍、轻量推荐、单次天气、交通或开放时间查询。\n  4  ---\n  5  \n  6  # 旅行规划\n  7  \n  8  生成真实可执行、路线合理、符合用户偏好的完整旅行计划。\n  9  \n 10  Main Agent 始终负责最终判断、最终规划和最终回答。\n 11  本 Skill 提供规划方法和输出规范，不定义固定 Workflow。\n 12  \n 13  ## 1. 理解旅行需求\n 14  \n 15  关注真正影响行程的信息：\n 16  \n 17  - 目的地与城市路线\n 18  - 日期或旅行天数\n 19  - 出发地与抵达 / 返程时间\n 20  - 旅行者组成及行动能力\n 21  - 预算\n 22  - 旅行风格与兴趣\n 23  - 交通偏好\n 24  - 必去 / 避开项目\n 25  - 住宿区域要求\n 26  - 其他明确约束\n 27  \n 28  不要把旅行规划变成问卷。\n 29  \n 30  如果已经知道目的地和可用日期 / 天数，通常直接开始规划。\n 31  对不会明显改变整体方案的信息采用合理假设。\n 32  只有缺失信息会显著改变整个行程、且无法安全假设时，才进行简洁追问。\n 33  \n 34  ## 2. Travel Researcher\n 35  \n 36  完整旅行规划天然需要多主题 Research。\n 37  \n 38  只要进入以下任一模式：\n 39  \n 40  - 创建完整旅行计划\n 41  - 重新规划完整旅行\n 42  - 修改已有完整旅行计划\n 43  \n 44  Main 必须调用：\n 45  \n 46  `task(subagent_type="travel-researcher", description="...")`\n 47  \n 48  由 Travel Researcher 在独立 Context 中完成所有与最终计划有关的外部 Research。\n 49  \n 50  固定链路：\n 51  \n 52  `Main → travel-planning Skill → Travel Researcher → Research Findings → Markdown Contract → Main Final Synthesis`\n 53  \n 54  规划模式下：\n 55  \n 56  - Main 不直接调用 `search_travel_info`\n 57  - Main 不直接调用 `search_maps`\n 58  - Main 不直接调用 `get_weather`\n 59  - Research 中间 Tool Result 留在 Travel Researcher Context\n 60  - Main 只接收 Research Findings\n 61  - 如果 Findings 有影响最终计划的关键缺口，继续委派 Travel Researcher 补充\n 62  \n 63  Travel Researcher 只负责 Research，不生成最终完整旅行计划。\n 64  \n 65  ### Research Brief\n 66  \n 67  Main 的委派描述必须自包含，至少包括：\n 68  \n 69  1. Runtime 当前日期、星期、时区、年份\n 70  2. 旅行背景\n 71  3. 用户约束\n 72  4. Research 目标\n 73  5. Research 范围\n 74  6. 当前信息的新鲜度要求\n 75  7. Anti-confirmation 要求\n 76  8. Research Findings 返回要求\n 77  9. “只做 Research、不生成最终计划”的职责边界\n 78  \n 79  普通旅行问答不是完整旅行规划，可由 Main 按需直接调用 Tool。\n 80  \n 81  ## 3. Research 新鲜度\n 82  \n 83  当前旅行事实必须以 Runtime 当前时间为基准。\n 84  \n 85  对于：\n 86  \n 87  - 门票 / Pass 价格\n 88  - 预约规则\n 89  - 开放 / 闭馆时间\n 90  - 当前运营状态\n 91  - 交通政策\n 92  - 节假日特殊安排\n 93  - 其他易变化事实\n 94  \n 95  Research 必须：\n 96  \n 97  - 优先 latest / current / official / 最新 / 当前 / 官方\n 98  - 用户未询问历史时，不主动使用旧年份\n 99  - 需要年份时使用 Runtime 当前年份\n100  - 旧资料不能直接当作当前事实\n101  - 无法确认时明确标记不确定性\n102  - 不把未经确认的模型猜测写进下一轮 Query 当作前提\n103  \n104  天气只在与实际旅行日期相关时 Research。\n105  没有实际旅行日期时，不应把“今天的天气”当作未来旅行计划依据。\n106  \n107  ## 4. 设计可执行路线\n108  \n109  优先：\n110  \n111  - 同区域活动集中安排\n112  - 减少跨区域往返\n113  - 避免明显回头路\n114  - 控制每天长距离移动\n115  - 给交通、排队、吃饭和休息留出真实时间\n116  - 根据旅行者情况调整强度\n117  - 保留必要缓冲\n118  \n119  亲子、老人或轻松旅行应降低强度并增加缓冲。\n120  高强度旅行可以提高活动密度，但仍必须保证实际可执行。\n121  \n122  相关情况下根据 Research Findings 检查：\n123  \n124  - 开放 / 关闭时间\n125  - 最晚入场时间\n126  - 固定闭馆日\n127  - 预约时间\n128  - 天气\n129  - 抵达 / 返程时间\n130  - 飞机 / 高铁时间\n131  - 城际交通\n132  - 排队时间\n133  \n134  不得生成明显存在时间冲突的行程。\n135  \n136  ## 5. 让预算参与规划\n137  \n138  根据预算调整：\n139  \n140  - 住宿\n141  - 城际交通\n142  - 当地交通\n143  - 景点与付费体验\n144  - 餐饮\n145  - 其他消费\n146  \n147  没有可靠价格时使用区间。\n148  不要编造未经验证的精确金额。\n149  若方案可能明显超预算，应主动调整或指出主要超支来源。\n150  \n151  ## 6. 创建完整旅行计划\n152  \n153  当用户明确要求生成完整旅行计划时：\n154  \n155  1. Main 理解需求，对非阻塞信息采用合理假设。\n156  2. 读取本 Skill。\n157  3. 必须委派 Travel Researcher。\n158  4. 等待 Research Findings 返回。\n159  5. Main 根据 conversation、用户约束和 Findings 完成最终路线与每日节奏。\n160  6. Research 完成后读取 `references/markdown-contract.md`。\n161  7. 严格按照 Markdown Contract 输出。\n162  8. 返回完整旅行计划，而不是 Research 摘要或景点清单。\n163  \n164  普通旅行问答不要读取 Markdown Contract。\n165  \n166  ## 7. 修改已有旅行计划\n167  \n168  当用户要求修改已有完整计划时：\n169  \n170  1. 将 conversation 中最近一次完整旅行计划视为当前版本。\n171  2. 理解用户真正想改变的内容。\n172  3. 保留未被修改的约束、偏好和有效安排。\n173  4. 必须委派 Travel Researcher Research 受影响的信息。\n174  5. Main 根据 Findings 检查时间、路线、交通和预算连锁影响。\n175  6. 必要时重新平衡其他日期。\n176  7. Research 完成后读取 `references/markdown-contract.md`。\n177  8. 返回新的完整 Markdown 旅行计划。\n178  \n179  不得只返回 Patch、Diff、修改项列表或单独修改后的某一天。\n180  \n181  普通解释性问题不是修改，直接回答即可。\n182  \n183  ## 8. 最终质量检查\n184  \n185  输出完整计划前确认：\n186  \n187  - 最新用户要求已体现\n188  - Runtime 时间已正确用于相对日期和当前信息判断\n189  - Research Findings 已返回\n190  - 天数和 Day 数量一致\n191  - 路线顺序合理\n192  - 没有明显折返\n193  - 主要交通时间现实\n194  - 抵达 / 返程时间合理\n195  - 开放、预约、天气等约束已考虑\n196  - 当前事实没有被旧年份资料错误替代\n197  - 没有把未经核验的猜测通过搜索“自证”\n198  - 预算没有明显违背用户要求\n199  - 没有伪造未经验证的精确事实\n200  - 用户明确要求没有遗漏\n201  - 修改时保留了未涉及内容\n202  - 最终结果是一份完整旅行计划\n203  \n204  不要创建额外 Validator Agent 或 Validator Workflow。\n205  \n206  ## 核心原则\n207  \n208  - 模糊、概率性的旅行判断交给 Main。\n209  - 当前日期和星期由 Runtime 动态提供。\n210  - 外部旅行事实由 Travel Researcher Research。\n211  - Research 中间上下文与 Main 最终规划上下文隔离。\n212  - Travel Researcher 只返回 Findings。\n213  - Main 是唯一最终旅行计划语义负责人。\n214  - 完整计划必须遵守 Markdown Contract。\n215  - 不得为了内容丰富而编造事实。\n216  - 优先保证旅行真实可执行，而不是增加景点数量。', name='read_file', id='a6b3d73f-5fd3-4c23-8ac7-40fb72c70ec7', tool_call_id='call_00_4J9moybM5Voyn9VlZNLi5773'),
                                              AIMessage(content='我已经读取了旅行规划技能。在开始规划之前，我需要确认几个关键信息，因为它们会显著影响整个行程方案。\n\n你提到"东京进"，这意味着从东京入境。我需要确认以下几点：\n\n1. **具体日期**：5天游大概是什么时候出发？（这会影响天气、樱花/红叶等季节因素）\n2. **返程城市**：是"东京进、东京出"，还是"东京进、其他城市出"（比如大阪/京都出）？这决定了是否需要跨城移动。\n3. **旅行风格**：你是想全程在东京及周边（如镰仓、箱根、富士山），还是想从东京去京都/大阪？\n4. **同行人**：一个人、情侣、朋友还是带家人？\n5. **预算**：大概的预算范围？\n\n不过，为了不让你觉得我在问一堆问题，我先做一个合理的假设来推进——**如果你只是想东京进、东京出，全程关东地区**，我可以直接开始规划。但如果你有跨城（比如去关西）的想法，请告诉我。\n\n让我先确认最关键的一点：\n\n**你这次5天是打算只在东京及周边玩，还是想从东京去京都/大阪（关西）？** 以及大概的出发日期和预算？\n\n如果你希望我直接按"东京进、东京出、全程关东"来规划，我现在就可以开始。请告诉我你的偏好，我马上安排。', additional_kwargs={'refusal': None}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 296, 'prompt_tokens': 6688, 'total_tokens': 6984, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cache_write_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 0}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 0, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 6688}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'fp_a18b46594c_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402', 'id': 'e4eedb23-173c-4fe6-a42f-b1caaa6f293f', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None}, name='travel_agent', id='lc_run--019fe579-719a-7711-8879-2334d24bdc46-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6688, 'output_tokens': 296, 'total_tokens': 6984, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}, 'output_token_details': {}}),
                                              HumanMessage(content='去大阪  8月26号', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='887d1fe1-7e85-4d00-bcbc-1ab378f79189'),
                                              AIMessage(content='明白了！你是**东京进、大阪出**，8月26号出发，5天游。这是一个经典的"东京进、大阪出"跨城路线。\n\n让我确认一下我的理解：\n- **8月26日**出发，5天（8/26 - 8/30）\n- **东京进**，**大阪出**（返程从大阪飞回）\n- 需要从东京到大阪的跨城移动（新干线）\n\n在开始规划前，我想再确认几个会影响方案的关键点，不过为了不拖沓，我先做合理假设，你可以随时纠正：\n\n1. **返程日期**：5天游，8/26出发，那么是 **8/30返程**（大阪出）对吧？\n2. **跨城方式**：我默认用**新干线**从东京到大阪（约2.5小时），这是最主流的方式。\n3. **旅行风格**：我默认是**中等强度、经典景点为主**的行程（东京2-3天 + 大阪1-2天，可能加京都）。\n4. **预算**：我默认**中档预算**。\n\n如果这些假设没问题，我现在就委派 Travel Researcher 去调研最新的交通、门票、开放时间等信息，然后为你生成完整行程。\n\n我先启动 Research。让我把详细的研究任务委派给 travel-researcher。', additional_kwargs={'refusal': None}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1131, 'prompt_tokens': 6995, 'total_tokens': 8126, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cache_write_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 1536}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 1536, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 5459}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'fp_a18b46594c_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402', 'id': 'b990933b-88d1-434a-a7e0-fb414b625f90', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None}, name='travel_agent', id='lc_run--019fe57a-3f32-7da3-b758-be449221105a-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'task', 'args': {'description': 'Research Brief for a 5-day Japan trip (Tokyo entry, Osaka exit).\n\n## Runtime time baseline\n- Current date: 2026-08-09 (Sunday)\n- Current time: 15:43 CST\n- Timezone: CST\n- Current year: 2026\n\n## Travel background\n- Trip: 5 days, departing 2026-08-26 (Wednesday), returning 2026-08-30 (Sunday).\n- Route: Fly into Tokyo (Narita or Haneda), travel to Osaka, fly out of Osaka (KIX or ITM).\n- 5-day itinerary spanning Tokyo and Osaka, likely with a day trip to Kyoto.\n- Cross-city transfer Tokyo→Osaka by Shinkansen (bullet train).\n\n## User constraints\n- 5 days total (Aug 26-30, 2026).\n- Tokyo entry, Osaka exit.\n- Default assumptions (to be validated): medium intensity, classic sights, mid-range budget, solo/couple travel.\n- Need realistic daily routing, transport times, and budget.\n\n## Research objectives\n1. Confirm current (2026) Shinkansen Tokyo→Osaka (Nozomi/Hikari) travel time, frequency, and approximate fare (standard reserved seat). Also whether JR Pass is worth it for this route (Tokyo-Osaka one-way + local travel).\n2. Current opening hours, last-entry times, fixed closing days, and any reservation requirements for major sights in Tokyo (e.g., Senso-ji, Meiji Shrine, Shibuya Sky, Tokyo Skytree, teamLab, Tokyo Disney if relevant) and Osaka (Osaka Castle, Dotonbori, Umeda Sky Building, Universal Studios Japan if relevant) and Kyoto (Fushimi Inari, Kiyomizu-dera, Kinkaku-ji, Arashiyama).\n3. Any 2026-specific operational notes, closures, or special events around late August (summer festival season, e.g., Tenjin Matsuri is July; check for late-August events).\n4. Weather/climate expectations for Tokyo and Osaka in late August (hot, humid, rainy season/typhoon risk) — for packing and pacing advice, not exact daily forecast.\n5. Airport transfer options and times: Narita/Haneda to central Tokyo; Osaka (KIX/ITM) to central Osaka.\n6. Approximate budget ranges for: Shinkansen fare, local transport (Suica/IC card), mid-range hotels in Tokyo and Osaka, and typical meal costs.\n\n## Research scope\n- Transport: Shinkansen Tokyo-Osaka, airport transfers, local transit.\n- Attractions: opening/closing times, last entry, fixed closed days, reservation needs, ticket/pass prices.\n- Seasonal: late-August weather/climate and any festivals or events.\n- Budget: fares, hotel ranges, meal costs.\n\n## Freshness requirements\n- Use Runtime date (2026-08-09) as baseline. Prefer latest/current/official sources. Do NOT use old-year data as current fact. Mark any uncertainty clearly. Do not treat unverified model guesses as established facts.\n\n## Anti-confirmation\n- Do NOT write unconfirmed prices, dates, or policies into your queries as if they were facts. Verify each claim from sources. If you cannot confirm a specific number, report a range or mark it as uncertain.\n\n## Return requirements\nReturn a structured Research Findings report with:\n- Key facts (with sources where possible)\n- Option comparisons (e.g., Shinkansen vs alternatives, JR Pass vs point-to-point)\n- Recommended tendencies\n- Conflicts/uncertainties clearly flagged\n- Time-sensitivity status of each fact\n- Budget ranges\n\n## Boundary\nYou are ONLY doing research. Do NOT generate the final full itinerary. Return Research Findings only.', 'subagent_type': 'travel-researcher'}, 'id': 'call_00_pqrTfhBQnqQmuZVa9j4k0801', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6995, 'output_tokens': 1131, 'total_tokens': 8126, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 1536}, 'output_token_details': {}}),
                                              ToolMessage(content='All my external research tools are failing:\n- `search_travel_info`: persistently returns `ForbiddenError` (plan usage limit exceeded) — completely unavailable.\n- `search_maps`: fails to geocode any location — completely unavailable.\n- `get_weather`: works (only tool available).\n\nI cannot verify current 2026 facts through live search. Per my instructions, I must not fabricate unverified prices, dates, or policies as established facts. I\'ll compile the Research Findings based on well-established, stable knowledge, clearly flagging what could not be live-verified and what is time-sensitive.\n\nLet me note the weather data I did obtain (current, not forecast for the trip dates).\n\nHere is my Research Findings report.\n\n---\n\n# Research Findings — Tokyo→Osaka 5-Day Trip (Aug 26–30, 2026)\n\n## ⚠️ Critical Tooling Note (read first)\n**Live verification was NOT possible during this research pass.**\n- `search_travel_info` (web search) returned `ForbiddenError: plan usage limit exceeded` on every attempt — **unavailable**.\n- `search_maps` (route/distance) failed to geocode all tested locations — **unavailable**.\n- Only `get_weather` functioned.\n\nConsequently, **no 2026-specific current facts could be confirmed from live sources.** The figures below are drawn from stable, long-standing baseline knowledge and must be treated as **unverified against 2026 sources**. Every time-sensitive item is flagged. **Do not treat any number below as a confirmed 2026 price/date/policy.** Re-run this research when the search tool is available before finalizing the itinerary.\n\n---\n\n## 关键事实 (Key Facts)\n\n### 1. Shinkansen Tokyo→Osaka (Tōkaidō Shinkansen)\n- **Travel time:** Nozomi ~2h30m; Hikari ~2h50m–3h; Kodama ~4h. *(stable, but 2026 schedule unverified)*\n- **Frequency:** Nozomi/Hikari run roughly every 10–15 min combined during peak. *(stable)*\n- **Fare (standard reserved seat, one-way):** approximately **¥14,500–¥15,000** (base fare + Nozomi/Hikari limited express surcharge). *(baseline knowledge; 2026 price unverified)*\n- **Note:** Nozomi is the fastest but is **not covered by the standard JR Pass** (only Hikari/Kodama are). This matters for JR Pass value math.\n\n### 2. JR Pass value for this route\n- **Standard JR Pass (7-day) price:** approximately **¥50,000** (2023-era price after the Oct 2023 increase; 2026 price unverified and likely higher).\n- **Math for this trip:** Tokyo→Osaka one-way Shinkansen (~¥15k) + local travel (Tokyo ~¥1–2k/day, Osaka ~¥1–2k/day) + optional Kyoto day trip round-trip (~¥1.5–2k local trains) ≈ **¥25k–¥30k total** without a pass.\n- **Conclusion (tendency):** A 7-day JR Pass (~¥50k+) is **almost certainly NOT worth it** for this 5-day, one-way Tokyo→Osaka itinerary. Point-to-point tickets + Suica/IC card is the cheaper, more flexible option. *(This is a strong, stable conclusion, but the 2026 pass price itself is unverified.)*\n\n### 3. Airport transfers\n- **Narita (NRT) → central Tokyo:** Skyliner (to Ueno/Nippori) ~36–41 min, ~¥2,500; Narita Express (N\'EX) ~60 min to Tokyo Station, ~¥3,000. *(baseline; 2026 fares unverified)*\n- **Haneda (HND) → central Tokyo:** Keikyu Line ~20–30 min to Shinagawa (~¥300–500); Tokyo Monorail ~15–20 min to Hamamatsucho (~¥500). Haneda is much closer/faster/cheaper than Narita. *(baseline)*\n- **Kansai (KIX) → central Osaka:** Haruka limited express ~50 min to Osaka/Shin-Osaka (~¥1,800–2,900); Nankai Rapi:t ~35–45 min to Namba (~¥1,500). *(baseline; unverified)*\n- **Itami (ITM) → central Osaka:** ~25–35 min by limousine bus or monorail+train (~¥600–1,500). *(baseline)*\n\n### 4. Weather / climate (late August)\n- **Current live readings (2026-08-09, for context only):** Tokyo 31°C (feels 33°C), humidity 58%; Osaka 33°C (feels 36°C), humidity 57%. Hot and humid.\n- **Late-August expectation (climate, not forecast):** Tokyo and Osaka are **hot (30–35°C), very humid**, with **high typhoon risk** (peak typhoon season is Aug–Sep) and frequent afternoon thunderstorms/showers. Rainy season (tsuyu) has ended by late August, but typhoon-related rain is a real risk.\n- **Pacing advice:** Plan indoor/air-conditioned activities for midday heat, hydrate, and build in flexibility for typhoon-related disruption (esp. to Shinkansen/flights). *(Climate-level, stable; exact daily forecast for Aug 26–30 cannot be predicted now.)*\n\n---\n\n## 当前预约 / 开放 / 门票 / Pass (Attractions — all UNVERIFIED for 2026)\n\n> **None of the following could be live-confirmed.** These are baseline operating norms and **must be re-verified** before finalizing.\n\n**Tokyo**\n- **Senso-ji (Asakusa):** Open daily, roughly 6:00–17:00 (main hall); grounds free. *(stable norm)*\n- **Meiji Shrine:** Open daily, roughly sunrise–sunset (approx 5:00–18:00 summer); free. *(stable norm)*\n- **Shibuya Sky:** Open ~9:00–22:00 (last entry ~21:00); **timed-entry ticket required**, book in advance. *(booking requirement stable; 2026 price unverified)*\n- **Tokyo Skytree:** Open ~10:00–21:00; timed tickets, book ahead. *(stable norm)*\n- **teamLab Planets / teamLab Borderless:** **Timed-entry tickets required**, book well in advance; Borderless reopened at Azabudai Hills (2023). *(booking requirement stable)*\n- **Tokyo Disney (if relevant):** Park tickets are **date-specific and often sell out**; must buy in advance. *(stable norm)*\n\n**Osaka**\n- **Osaka Castle:** Open daily ~9:00–17:00 (last entry 16:30); museum admission ~¥600. *(stable norm)*\n- **Dotonbori:** Outdoor area, always open; free.\n- **Umeda Sky Building (Kuchu Teien Observatory):** Open ~9:30–22:30 (last entry 22:00); ~¥1,500. *(stable norm)*\n- **Universal Studios Japan (if relevant):** **Date-specific tickets + timed entry**; crowded in summer; buy in advance. *(stable norm)*\n\n**Kyoto (day trip)**\n- **Fushimi Inari:** Open 24h, free; best early morning to avoid crowds.\n- **Kiyomizu-dera:** Open ~6:00–18:00 (summer); ~¥400–500.\n- **Kinkaku-ji:** Open ~9:00–17:00; ~¥500.\n- **Arashiyama (Bamboo Grove):** Open 24h, free; best early morning.\n\n---\n\n## 路线 / 交通比较 (Route / Transport Comparison)\n\n| Option | Time | Approx Cost | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Shinkansen Nozomi** Tokyo→Osaka | ~2h30m | ~¥14.5–15k | Fastest; NOT covered by standard JR Pass |\n| **Shinkansen Hikari** | ~2h50m–3h | ~¥14.5k | Covered by JR Pass |\n| **JR Pass (7-day)** | — | ~¥50k+ | Not worth it for this one-way trip |\n| **Flight Tokyo→Osaka** | ~1h15m + airport time | ~¥8–15k | Not worth it given airport overhead; Shinkansen simpler |\n| **Bus (overnight)** | ~8h | ~¥5–8k | Cheapest but slow; not recommended for 5-day trip |\n\n**Tendency:** **Shinkansen point-to-point (Nozomi) + Suica/IC card** is the recommended transport setup. Skip the JR Pass.\n\n---\n\n## 推荐倾向及理由 (Recommended Tendencies)\n1. **Transport:** Buy point-to-point Shinkansen (Nozomi) + Suica/IC card. Skip JR Pass (not cost-effective for one-way + local travel).\n2. **Airports:** Prefer **Haneda** for entry (much closer/faster/cheaper to central Tokyo than Narita). For Osaka exit, **KIX** is fine (Haruka to Osaka); ITM is closer but has fewer international flights.\n3. **Kyoto day trip:** Feasible as a day trip from Osaka (~30–40 min by local train from Osaka/Umeda to Kyoto). Prioritize early-morning Fushimi Inari + one or two other sights to keep it realistic.\n4. **Pacing:** Given late-August heat/humidity, plan midday indoor breaks and keep the daily route compact.\n\n---\n\n## 冲突 / 不确定性 (Conflicts / Uncertainties)\n- **HIGH — All 2026 prices, opening hours, and policies are UNVERIFIED.** The web search tool was unavailable, so nothing was confirmed against current sources. Treat every number as a baseline estimate.\n- **HIGH — JR Pass 2026 price** unknown; the "not worth it" conclusion is robust to reasonable price changes but the pass price itself is unconfirmed.\n- **MEDIUM — Typhoon risk** in late August could disrupt Shinkansen/flights; exact forecast for Aug 26–30 cannot be predicted now.\n- **MEDIUM — Attraction closing days:** Most major sights are open daily, but some (e.g., certain museums, teamLab) have irregular closures; unverified for 2026.\n- **LOW — Shinkansen schedule** (times/frequency) is stable but 2026 timetable not confirmed.\n\n---\n\n## 重要来源 (Sources)\n- **None available this pass.** All `search_travel_info` and `search_maps` calls failed (plan usage limit / geocoding failure). Only `get_weather` returned data (live Tokyo/Osaka readings on 2026-08-09).\n- Recommended official sources to verify when search is restored: JR Central (Tōkaidō Shinkansen), JR East/JR West, official attraction sites (Shibuya Sky, Skytree, teamLab, USJ, Tokyo Disney), and JR Pass official site.\n\n---\n\n## 时效状态 (Time-Sensitivity Status)\n| Fact | Time-sensitivity | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shinkansen fare/times | High | **Unverified for 2026** |\n| JR Pass price | High | **Unverified for 2026** |\n| Airport transfer fares | Medium | **Unverified for 2026** |\n| Attraction hours/prices | High | **Unverified for 2026** |\n| Late-August climate (heat/humidity/typhoon) | Low (climate) | Stable baseline; exact forecast N/A |\n| Live weather (Aug 9) | — | Confirmed (Tokyo 31°C, Osaka 33°C) |\n\n---\n\n## 预算范围 (Budget Ranges — all UNVERIFIED estimates)\n- **Shinkansen Tokyo→Osaka (Nozomi, reserved):** ~¥14,500–15,000\n- **Local transport (Suica/IC), per day:** ~¥1,000–2,000\n- **Mid-range hotels, Tokyo & Osaka, per night:** ~¥12,000–20,000 (per room)\n- **Meals, per person per day:** ~¥3,000–6,000 (casual–mid-range)\n- **Attraction tickets (major sights):** ~¥500–2,500 each; teamLab/Sky/USJ higher (¥2,000–8,000+)\n\n---\n\n## Bottom Line for Main Agent\n- **Route is feasible and standard:** Tokyo (2–3 days) → Shinkansen → Osaka (2–3 days) with a Kyoto day trip.\n- **Use point-to-point Shinkansen + Suica; skip the JR Pass.**\n- **Prefer Haneda for entry.**\n- **Plan for heat/humidity and possible typhoon disruption.**\n- **⚠️ CRITICAL:** All 2026-specific facts are **unverified** because the web search tool was down during this pass. **Re-run this research with `search_travel_info` restored before finalizing prices, hours, and booking requirements.**', name='task', id='c8d96eaf-7fe3-4065-baa1-1ca451fc1370', tool_call_id='call_00_pqrTfhBQnqQmuZVa9j4k0801'),
                                              AIMessage(content='Travel Researcher 已经返回了调研结果。不过有一个重要情况需要向你说明：**本次调研的联网工具暂时不可用**，所以很多具体的价格、开放时间等时效性信息无法通过实时搜索确认，只能基于稳定的常识给出参考值。\n\n我先读取 Markdown Contract，然后为你生成一份完整行程。同时，我会在计划中明确标注哪些信息需要你在出行前核实。', additional_kwargs={'refusal': None}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 138, 'prompt_tokens': 11022, 'total_tokens': 11160, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cache_write_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 1536}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 1536, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 9486}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'fp_a18b46594c_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402', 'id': 'c2834653-b98a-4221-8aee-693eb998f986', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None}, name='travel_agent', id='lc_run--019fe57b-01a5-71b2-a007-4074976cf47c-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'read_file', 'args': {'file_path': '/skills/travel-planning/references/markdown-contract.md'}, 'id': 'call_00_5m7DfVpslN3otWKeI7Em1212', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11022, 'output_tokens': 138, 'total_tokens': 11160, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 1536}, 'output_token_details': {}}),
                                              ToolMessage(content='  1  # Travel Plan Markdown Contract\n  2  \n  3  本文件定义完整旅行计划的固定 Markdown 输出协议。\n  4  \n  5  ## 1. 核心规则\n  6  \n  7  完整旅行计划的核心标题属于稳定 Contract：\n  8  \n  9  - 标题名称不得修改\n 10  - 不得用同义标题替代\n 11  - 不得添加 Emoji\n 12  - 不得改变标题层级\n 13  - 不得把两个核心模块合并\n 14  \n 15  内容可以灵活，核心结构必须稳定。\n 16  \n 17  ## 2. 标准结构\n 18  \n 19  ```markdown\n 20  # {目的地}{天数}旅行计划\n 21  \n 22  ## 行程概览\n 23  \n 24  - 日期 / 天数：\n 25  - 旅行者：\n 26  - 旅行风格：\n 27  - 核心路线：\n 28  - 预算定位：\n 29  \n 30  ## 行前准备\n 31  \n 32  - 大交通：\n 33  - 天气：\n 34  - 住宿区域：\n 35  - 当地交通：\n 36  - 预约事项：\n 37  - 必备物品：\n 38  \n 39  ## Day 1｜{主题 / 区域}\n 40  \n 41  ### 上午\n 42  \n 43  ...\n 44  \n 45  ### 下午\n 46  \n 47  ...\n 48  \n 49  ### 晚上\n 50  \n 51  ...\n 52  \n 53  ### 交通\n 54  \n 55  ...\n 56  \n 57  ### 费用\n 58  \n 59  ...\n 60  \n 61  ### 提醒\n 62  \n 63  ...\n 64  \n 65  ## Day 2｜{主题 / 区域}\n 66  \n 67  ...\n 68  \n 69  ## 住宿建议\n 70  \n 71  ...\n 72  \n 73  ## 美食建议\n 74  \n 75  ...\n 76  \n 77  ## 预算参考\n 78  \n 79  ...\n 80  \n 81  ## 出行提醒\n 82  \n 83  ...\n 84  ```\n 85  \n 86  ## 3. 固定标题\n 87  \n 88  必须使用：\n 89  \n 90  ```markdown\n 91  ## 行程概览\n 92  ## 行前准备\n 93  ## 住宿建议\n 94  ## 美食建议\n 95  ## 预算参考\n 96  ## 出行提醒\n 97  ```\n 98  \n 99  不得使用同义标题替代\n100  \n\n[Read 100 lines (lines 1-100 of 223 total). 123 lines remaining from offset 100.]', name='read_file', id='650a36de-1053-4a51-b0ec-f12127b0ceac', tool_call_id='call_00_5m7DfVpslN3otWKeI7Em1212'),
